WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:14.192
A suspected spy got close to the boss of Nvidia. Within days,
hundreds of billions of dollars vanished. So we built our own secret AI chip vault. Ten chips. One billion-dollar company. And one of us is a spy. By sunrise, somebody's going to lose everything.

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:32.500
Quick recap, because this is real. A Chinese executive named Alice Huang, no relation, was reportedly watched by US intelligence,
which allegedly concluded she was a Chinese asset. Her calls reportedly turned up the name of Nvidia's CEO, Jensen Huang. Reportedly, he was never warned.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:55.256
Then the story broke. He told his employees he had been unfaithful, the board opened an independent investigation,
and the stock plunged by hundreds of billions. Nobody has been charged, China denies it, and Nvidia says the relationship wasn't unusual.
We're not accusing anyone of anything. We're asking one question: what would YOU do if a spy was already inside your company?

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:10.448
We have two hours. Laser-grid made of string. A keypad. A fake fingerprint scanner. We're feeling invincible.
Our company is worth $5.78 billion. Look at this scoreboard.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:23.384
We leave to eat. We come back. Chip number three is gone.

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:41.392
The scoreboard drops to $4.78 billion. Nobody saw anything.
And the spy is looking at us, smiling, nodding, acting shocked.

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:52.624
One chip gone. Nine left. The scoreboard says $4.78 billion,
and the spy is standing right here with us.

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:03.320
The alarm is screaming. Everybody up, the vault has been hit!

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:12.560
We count the chips. Nine left.
One is missing, and nobody saw a thing.

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:21.000
Then it gets worse. We blame the wrong person.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:30.056
Two more chips disappear. $2.78 billion.
Trust meter: zero.

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:38.664
Our friend cries, honestly, because we accused him.

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:48.632
Three chips gone. The game is falling apart,
and the spy is still standing right here.

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:54.064
I was sleeping! I didn't take anything!

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:05.144
We stop guessing. We hunt.
Every clue on the board, every thread, we follow them all.

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:14.472
We replay the CCTV. Frame by frame.
Somebody walked past that camera, and we missed it.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:23.568
Move one: bring in an outsider. A neutral judge.
He investigates everyone, including me.

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:30.776
I question everyone. No exceptions. Not even the host.

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:37.856
Move two: tell your team first. I accused the wrong person, on camera.
That was my fault.

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:44.752
Move three: rebuild in layers. Two-person rule,
nobody opens the vault alone.

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:55.736
Move four: test it in public. Try to steal a chip while everyone watches.
It's a game, a general playbook. And the board is climbing: $4.1 billion.

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:04.424
The board says $4.1 billion. But trust? Trust is still broken.

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:12.232
One final night. One last chance for the spy.
The clock is running, and the card is on the table.

